wifi: ath11k: compare the RX packet header TLV with the MPDU start descriptor

The 802.11 header of a received frame is read from the 128 byte packet
header TLV of the RX descriptor for every frame that goes back to
mac80211 as 802.11 (EAPOL, group-addressed frames, which also take the
CCMP header from it for the replay check in mac80211, native Wi-Fi
decapsulation, frames from another source than the peer). The MPDU start
descriptor also holds the frame control, duration, addresses, sequence
control, QoS control, HT control and the PN and key ID of the MPDU, so
the TLV, which the firmware can leave out with the RX ring selection
configuration, could be replaced by a header built from it.

Whether the descriptor holds all of that for every MSDU of an A-MPDU and
of an A-MSDU, and in the format the CCMP header needs, is not documented,
so add a check that finds it out on a device: with the new
ath11k.rx_hdr_check module parameter every received MSDU of an IPQ8074
radio has its header TLV compared field by field with the descriptor, and
the differences are counted per field, for the first MSDU of an MPDU and
for the others, in the soc_dp_stats debugfs file. Nothing changes for
the frame.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
